          %title Contents
          %blockquote
            %p
              This entry is about discontinuities in parameter dependence of (often asymptotic) solutions of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+equations"} differential equations
              and similar phenomena (notably in the context of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+states"} BPS states
              formalized via
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bridgeland+stability+conditions"} Bridgeland stability conditions
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
              which are often interpreted as crossing the walls of marginal stability in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morse+theory"} Morse theory
              see at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cerf+wall+crossing"} Cerf wall crossing
              and for the (Weyl chamber wall) crossing functors in representation theory see
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wall+crossing+functor"} wall crossing functor
          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#overview"} Overview
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#in_supersymmetric_field_theory"} In supersymmetric field theory
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#introductions_and_lectures"} Introductions and lectures
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#original_articles"} Original articles
                %ul
                  %li
                    %a{:href => "#general"} General
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#in_supergravity"} In supergravity
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#conferences_and_seminars"} Conferences and seminars
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#categorification"} Categorification
          %h2#overview Overview
          %p
            In the study of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solitons"} solitons
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WKB+approximation"} WKB-style approximation
            to a nonlinear
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+equation"} wave equation
            (see also
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eikonal+equation"} eikonal equation
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maslov+index"} Maslov index
            = succeed "." do
              %strong Stokes lines
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stokes+phenomenon"} Stokes phenomenon
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomonodromic+deformation"} isomonodromic deformation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ODEs"} ODEs
            in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+plane"} complex plane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/soliton"} soliton
            theory, and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrable+systems"} integrable systems
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Painlev%C3%A9+transcendent"} Painlevé transcendent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Masaki+Kashiwara"} Kashiwara
            etc.), including the use of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-modules"} D-modules
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/microlocal+analysis"} microlocal analysis
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holonomic+quantum+field"} holonomic quantum field
          %p
            The solutions of meromorphic differential equations can be expressed in terms of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meromorphic+connection"} meromorphic connection
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-module"} modules
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+theory"} Hodge theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+spaces"} moduli spaces
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck"} Grothendieck
            has shown how to correctly define and construct some fundamental
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+spaces"} moduli spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+sheaves"} coherent sheaves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Mumford"} David Mumford
            who geometrized classical invariant theory into
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+invariant+theory"} geometric invariant theory
            %span.newWikiWord
              Castelnuovo-Mumford regularity
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Castelnuovo-Mumford+regularity"} ?
            (cf.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castelnuovo%E2%80%93Mumford_regularity"} wikipedia
          %h3#in_supersymmetric_field_theory In supersymmetric field theory
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Yang-Mills+theory"} super Yang-Mills theory
            the number of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+states"} BPS states
            is locally constant as a function of the parameters of the theory, but it may jump at certain “walls” in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+spaces"} moduli spaces
            of parameters. The precise behaviour of the BPS states as one crosses these walls is studied as “wall crossing phenomena”.
          %p
            Another example are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+spaces"} moduli spaces
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higgs+bundles"} Higgs bundles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carlos+Simpson"} Carlos Simpson
            and others, which have special cases with interpretations both in geometry and in the gauge theory (instantons). It appears that sometimes they can be linked to the geometric picture.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann-Hilbert+correspondence"} Riemann-Hilbert correspondence
          %p
            Surely, one often works at the derived level. An adaptation of the notion of stability into the setup of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+categories"} triangulated categories
            has been introduced by Bridgeland. Bridgeland stability for the derived categories of (boundary conditions of) D-branes (B-model) are relevant for string theory.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+state"}> BPS state
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-module"} D-module
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cluster+algebra"} cluster algebra
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver"} quiver
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theory
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Donaldson-Thomas+invariant"} Donaldson-Thomas invariant
          %div
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th singularity
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+theory+with+singularities"} field theory with singularities
              %tbody
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+condition"}> boundary condition
                    \/
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane"} brane
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theory"} boundary field theory
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain+wall"}> domain wall
                    \/
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bi-brane"} bi-brane
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QFT+with+defects"} QFT with defects
          %h2#references References
          %h3#introductions_and_lectures Introductions and lectures
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergio+Cecotti"}> Sergio Cecotti
                ,
                %em Trieste lectures on wall-crossing invariants
                (2010) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://people.sissa.it/~cecotti/ictptext.pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Greg+Moore"}> Greg Moore
                ,
                %em
                  PiTP Lectures on BPS states and wall-crossing in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi d
                          %mo =
                          %mn 4
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 4
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒩
                        %mo =
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N} = 2
                  theories
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.physics.rutgers.edu/~gmoore/PiTP_July26_2010.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Dimofte10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tudor+Dimofte"}> Tudor Dimofte
                ,
                %em Refined wall crossing
                (
                %a{:href => "http://thesis.library.caltech.edu/5808/4/TD_part1.pdf"}> pdf
                ), part I of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Refined BPS invariants, Chern-Simons theory, and the quantum dilogarithm
